    "summary": "High‑energy set with soaring Dark Star, crisp Bird Song and stellar Bass",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a monster Dark Star > Weather Report Suite Prelude marathon, a tight Box of Rain → Playing In The Band flow and gorgeous Bird Song. Phil’s bass shines throughout, especially on the extended jams. A solid second‑set climax with Stella Blue and Sugar Magnolia rounds out an inspired night.",
    "review": "The November 19, 1972 concert at Houston's Hofheinz Pavilion captures the Dead in a rare bout of pure inspiration. From the opening Bertha through a flawless Me & My Uncle lyric twist, the first set builds momentum with Bird Song and Black Throated Wind before launching into a seamless Box of Rain → Playing In The Band sequence that sets up a high‑octane second set. Dark Star erupts into a 20‑minute odyssey that morphs into the Weather Report Suite Prelude, showcasing Jerry’s soaring leads and Phil’s thunderous solo, while Keith adds playful piano teases. The night closes with an emotive Stella Blue, a rollicking Sugar Magnolia and a rousing Goin’ Down The Road Feeling Bad, leaving the band locked in and the audience riding the wave.",
